                <pb facs="1051" n="893" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg893"/>

                <head>[Inclosure.—Translation.]</head>
                <p>By the advice of the department of finance, dated September 27, 1905, published
                    in the Moniteurs Nos. 7 and 11 in October of the same year, the public and
                    commerce were informed that the council of secretaries of state had decided that
                    the law authorizing the opening of the port of the Mole St. Nicholas to all
                    foreign commerce would be executed after the formation of the administrative
                    force of the above-named place.</p>
                <p>The public and commerce are advised that the said port is open to all foreign
                    commerce, His Excellency the President of the Republic having named the
                    administrative force for the offices of the finance department and the customs
                    service.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-10-04"><hi rendition="#italic">October 4,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
